<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch2-chapter-first-full-investigation" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>The Statistical Investigation Process</title>
  

  <introduction>
    <p> This chapter will introduce students to the big ideas that they will learn in this course through the examination of a full
      statistical investigation. There will be a focus on introducing all of the main vocabulary that will be used. The chapter will 
      end with a discussion of what makes a "good" research question.  </p>
  </introduction>

